  "title": "Emergence cannot be brute",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "293633c8-0167-464a-891f-6a06a12aa052",
      "text": "If Y truly emerges from X, there must be something about X, and X alone, in virtue of which Y emerges and which suffices for Y. Brute emergence, with no reason in the nature of things, would be a miracle each time it occurred, and a lawlike miracle is a contradiction.",
